fact WorkItem(id: "WI-914", description: some(value: "`anthill query --mode sort|functor|domain` (anthill-cli/src/main.rs ~1370/1380/1389) looks its USER-SUPPLIED argument up by absolute name only, while `--mode pattern` resolves the same text through the shared ladder at `_global`. So `--mode functor Map.empty` cannot name what `--mode pattern 'Map.empty()'` names — the WI-752 headline divergence, one layer up, on the same CLI. This is a DECISION TO RE-EXAMINE, not an assumed bug: the comment at ~1345 states the current reading deliberately ('a listing mode looks its argument up by name, not in the query scope'). WI-908 makes the counter-argument concrete — every other position that reads KB-EXTERNAL text now runs one ladder, and a CLI argument is the most external text there is; a user who can write `-i` (WI-853, a top-level import into `_global`) has said which names they mean. NOT DRIVEN. FIRST STEP: drive the divergence — with `-i`, compare `--mode functor <short>` against `--mode pattern` on the same name. ACCEPTANCE: the two modes agree on what a name denotes, or the comment at ~1345 states why a listing mode is a different QUESTION (as `DottedVisibility::Any`'s documented exception does) rather than merely a different lookup; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-01T08:13:15Z"))
